(391, 103, 717, 635, 1, 'A guy who, due to his shape, is often asked, ‘Would you play Santa this Christmas?’. Philippe Laprise!', NULL),
(392, 103, 717, 634, 2, 'She looks like the Star Fairy. I’ll let you figure out if that’s a compliment. Marie-Soleil Dion!', 'The <a target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://www.cbc.ca/news/canada/montreal/quebec-star-fairy-history-1.7399979\">Star Fairy</a> helps Santa Claus, in French-Canadian lore.'),
(393, 103, 717, 636, 3, 'He looks like a guy who\'ll wait for the 31 at midnight to get some sparkling wine: Stéphane Rousseau!', 'The 31 is a Montreal city bus route.'),
(394, 103, 717, 632, 4, 'She entered our screens through the front door, not the chimney. Fabiola Aladin!', NULL),
(395, 103, 717, 633, 5, 'Unlike a sandwich loaf, her comedic talent is uncontroversial. Genevieve Schmidt!', 'A <a target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sandwich_loaf\">sandwich loaf</a> is a stacked savoury party entrée made from a loaf of horizontally sliced bread, and is popular in Quebec during the holidays.'),
(396, 107, 701, 624, 1, 'The show host’s show host: Pär Lernström.', 'Pär is the host of several TV competition shows, including <em>Swedish Idol</em>, <em>Sweden’s Got Talent</em>, and <em>Masterchef Sweden</em>.'),
(397, 107, 701, 622, 2, 'The most awesome one in ‘Grotesco’: Hanna Dorsin.', 'Grotesco is a comedy group which also includes former Bäst i Test guest contestants <a href=\"/person.php?id=94\">Per Andersson</a> and <a href=\"/person.php?id=96\">Emma Molin</a>. '),
(398, 107, 701, 623, 3, 'The one from ‘Leif & Billy’: Klas Eriksson.', '<em><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://sv.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leif_%26_Billy\">Leif & Billy</a></em> is a comedy show about two dim and unemployed brothers living in Northern Sweden. Klas plays Leif, while season 10 contestant <a href=\"/person.php?id=647\">Alfred Svensson</a> plays Billy.'),
(399, 107, 701, 625, 4, 'Viktor’s best buddy: Samir Badran.', 'Samir makes up one half of the singing duo Samir & Viktor, alongside fashion blogger <a target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Samir_%26_Viktor\">Viktor Frisk</a>. '),
(400, 107, 701, 626, 5, 'Sune’s mother: Sissela Benn.', 'Sissela played the mother of a young male character named Sune Andersson in a series of films based on the ‘<a target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://sv.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sunes_universum\">Sunes universum</a>’ (‘Sune’s universe’) series of books.'),
(401, 104, 730, 648, 1, 'Three-time Melodifestivalen host: Gina Dirawi.', '<a target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Melodifestivalen\">Melodifestivalen</a> is the televised annual competition through which Sweden’s entry to the <a target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eurovision_Song_Contest\">Eurovision Song Contest</a> is chosen. '),
(402, 104, 730, 647, 2, 'Billy from ‘Leif & Billy’: Alfred Svensson.', '<em><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://sv.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leif_%26_Billy\">Leif & Billy</a></em> is a comedy show about two dim and unemployed brothers living in Northern Sweden. Alfred plays Billy, while former contestant <a href=\"/person.php?id=623\">Klas Eriksson</a> plays Leif.'),
(403, 104, 730, 650, 3, 'The taxi driver from ‘c/o Segemyhr’: Olle Sarri.', '<em><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://sv.wikipedia.org/wiki/C/o_Segemyhr\">c/o Segemyhr</a></em> was a late ‘90s / early ‘00s sitcom on TV4. Olle played Aton, a shy taxi driver with dreams of stardom.'),
(404, 104, 730, 202, 4, '‘Hey Baberiba’ with the family: Christine Meltzer.', '<em><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://sv.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hey_Baberiba\">Hey Baberiba</a></em> was a sketch comedy show which Christine co-created and starred in, and which often lampooned the Swedish royal family.'),
(405, 104, 730, 649, 5, 'The fragrant madman: Jan Rippe.', 'This is likely a reference to Jan’s membership of the comedy group and barbershop quartet collective <a target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://sv.wikipedia.org/wiki/Galenskaparna_och_After_Shave\">Galenskaparna och After Shave</a> (‘The Madness and After Shave’), of which episode guest Per Fritzell is also a member.'),
(406, 104, 731, 648, 1, 'Gina with a ‘G’, not Gina with a ‘J’, Dirawi!', NULL),
(407, 104, 731, 647, 2, 'The countryside romantic, Alfred Svensson!', NULL),
(408, 104, 731, 650, 3, '‘Heja Björn’ in the flesh, Olle Sarri!', 'Olle played Björn in the 2002 Swedish TV comedy series <em><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://sv.wikipedia.org/wiki/Heja_Bj%C3%B6rn\">Heja Björn</a></em>.'),
(409, 104, 731, 202, 4, '50% of ‘Berg & Meltzer’, Christine Meltzer!', 'Christine has co-presented a series of TV shows with <a href=\"/person.php?id=406\">Carina Berg</a> under the duo naming of ‘Berg & Meltzer’.'),
(410, 104, 731, 649, 5, 'And the former petrol station owner, Jan Rippe!', 'Jan played the role of petrol station co-owner Roger in <em><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://sv.wikipedia.org/wiki/Macken\">Macken</a></em>, a six-part Swedish musical sitcom from 1986, produced by his musical comedy collective <a target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://sv.wikipedia.org/wiki/Galenskaparna_och_After_Shave\">Galenskaparna och After Shave</a>.'),
(411, 104, 732, 648, 1, 'The supernova from Sundsvall: Gina Dirawi.', NULL),
(412, 104, 732, 647, 2, 'The vacillator from Vimmerby: Alfred Svensson.', NULL),
