(604, 102, 750, 656, 1, 'She’s an influencer. She’s a commentator. She’s so proud of her bad temper, and there’s nothing cuter than subjecting a person with such a bad temper to a merry-go-round of tasks which, under normal conditions, she would never do. But she will. Give it up for Pipoca Mais Doce, Ana Garcia Martins!', 'Pipoca is the author of the lifestyle blog, <em>A Pipoca Mais Doce</em> (‘The Sweetest Popcorn’), which is often cited as the most-read blog in Portugal. She is frequently addressed by the nickname ‘Pipoca’ (‘Popcorn’) instead of her given name Ana.'),
(605, 102, 750, 328, 2, 'A Taskmaster veteran. Basically, he’s an explosive fusion of thoroughness, agility, and dozens of other bizarre things even he didn’t know he was capable of. He came from Angola and made his home in our hearts. The man known as Mr. Fila da Goda. Your love for Gilmário Vemba!', '‘Fila da Goda’ is an Angolan expression meaning ‘son of a bitch’. It is also Gilmário’s <a target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://www.instagram.com/mr_filadagodaaa/\">Instagram handle</a>.'),
(606, 102, 750, 442, 3, 'Taskmaster royalty. An actress who has already left here with my head under her arm. I had to ask her to let go of it, because she was meant to take the gold one, but… she was trying to take my actual head. She went viral amid an ocean of shoes. “IS IT THIS ONE?!” It’s Gabriela Barros!', 'Vasco is referring to Gabriela’s legendary attempt at the ‘<a href=\"/task.php?id=3289\">Guess Shoe</a>’ task in season 3, episode 5. '),
(607, 102, 750, 657, 4, 'A comedian of so many faces and so much personality, all in one. Some days he’s Zeca Estacionâncio, other days he’s Bino. For us, he’s kind of a living cartoon. His name is Pedro Alves!', '‘Zeca Estacionâncio’ is Pedro’s on-stage alter-ego character in a comedy duo with João Paulo Rodrigues (stage name ‘Quim Roscas’). The character was conceived for the ‘Curral Social’ comedy segment of the Portuguese morning show <em>Praça da Alegria</em>, and rose in popularity after the segment span off into  an independent parody news show, called <em>Telerural</em>, which spawned international live shows, a book (<em>Curral de Moinas em Busca da Cadela Perdida</em>) and two movies (<em>7 Pecados Rurais</em>, <em>Curral de Moinas – Os banqueiros do Povo</em>). Albino ‘Bino’ Jesus is the character Pedro plays on the telenovela series <em><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://pt.wikipedia.org/wiki/Festa_%C3%89_Festa\">Festa é Festa</a></em>.'),
(608, 102, 750, 663, 5, 'And our guest tonight: the tiny Isabela Valadeiro!', 'Vasco is being ironic, since Isabela is actually quite tall, at 180cm / 5’10”.'),
(609, 102, 754, 656, 1, 'Applause for Ana Garcia ‘Pipoca Mais Doce’ Martins!', 'Ana’s social media brand name is <a target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://www.instagram.com/apipocamaisdoce/\">Pipoca Mais Doce</a> (‘The Sweetest Popcorn’), and she is more often referred to by her nickname, Pipoca (‘Popcorn’) because of this.'),
(610, 102, 754, 328, 2, 'Applause for Gilmario ‘Filadagoda’ Vemba!', '‘Filadagoda’ is an Angolan slang term for ‘son of a bitch’, and is also Gilmario’s <a target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://www.instagram.com/mr_filadagodaaa/\">Instagram handle</a> (with a few extra ‘A’s). '),
(611, 102, 754, 442, 3, 'Your love for Gabriela ‘IS THIS IT?!’ Barros!', 'Vasco is referring to Gabriela’s legendary attempt at the ‘<a href=\"/task.php?id=3289\">Guess Shoe</a>’ task in season 3, episode 5, from which her increasingly desperate cries of “IS THIS IT?!” became a meme in Portugal.'),
(612, 102, 754, 657, 4, 'Kudos to Pedro ‘For the love of god, stop calling me Bino’ Alves!', 'Pedro plays Albino ‘Bino’ Jesus on the telenovela <em><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://pt.wikipedia.org/wiki/Festa_%C3%89_Festa\">Festa é Festa</a></em> (‘Life is a Party’).'),
(613, 102, 754, 682, 5, 'Our special guest is called André Filipe Alves Monteiro, but the whole world knows him as King Ukra!', '<a target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://pt.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ukra\">Ukra</a> is known largely by his nickname, given to him in his youth due to his thin blonde hair giving him the appearance of someone from the Ukraine, which was then shortened to ‘Ukra’.'),
(614, 99, 745, 577, 1, 'The dynamic Dave Hughes.', NULL),
(615, 99, 745, 578, 2, 'The electric Emma Holland.', NULL),
(616, 99, 745, 579, 3, 'The lyrical Lisa McCune.', NULL),
(617, 99, 745, 580, 4, 'The winsome Waka.', NULL),
(618, 99, 745, 581, 5, 'The tenacious Tommy Little.', NULL),
(619, 57, 461, 329, 1, 'She shouts, she riots, she’s competitive, she’s a sore loser. But in the end, her laughter’s the sweetest. And the entire country laughs with her. She’s shown that she’s mastered the art of fountains, the art of twerking, and she rents aeroplanes with messages about Nuno Markl’s nightly urine. Applause for the extraordinary Inês Aires Pereira!', 'Vasco is specifically referring to Inês’ attempts at the ‘<a href=\"/task.php?id=1852\">Create an impressive fountain</a>’ and ‘<a href=\"/task.php?id=3109\">Do the worst thing and make the best apology</a>’ tasks, as well as Inês’ tendency to twerk in the studio to celebrate her victories.'),
(620, 57, 461, 328, 2, 'Someone who, before season 1, was a stranger to a lot of Portuguese people. Now, dear god, no-one can stop this man. And it’s only fair that people surrender to the talent of this young man. But it’s not just his talent. It’s also his kindness, his good manners. And, if he gained notoriety from Taskmaster, then damn it, Taskmaster also gained a lot from him. Applause for the amazing Gilmário Vemba!', NULL),
(621, 57, 461, 330, 3, 'We saw this girl become a woman before our very eyes. Gone are the days of Mimi from Morangos. Now Jessica’s showing her worth in soap operas, in series, in movies, and also here at Taskmaster. Her first ideas don’t always end up working. But her disappointed faces on this second series are the proof that she gives her all on this show. And I’m so glad for that. It’s the wonderful Jessica Athayde!', '<a target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://pt.wikipedia.org/wiki/Morangos_com_A%C3%A7%C3%BAcar\">Morangos com Açúcar</a> (‘Strawberries with Sugar’) was a Portuguese teen drama in which Jessica appeared between 2005 and 2007.'),
(622, 57, 461, 327, 4, 'A man I know from way back. But who would’ve thought that Taskmaster would show that this man is capable of doing a little bit of everything. He wrecked watermelons. He strolled nearly-naked in Margem Sul. He did it all without ever thinking twice. And I’m glad he also didn’t think twice when we invited him to be part of this. He’s the kind of guy that, if you befriend him, you’ve got a friend for life. The only, the one, the extraordinary Toy!', '<a target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://pt.wikipedia.org/wiki/Margem_Sul\">Margem Sul</a> is a part of Lisbon that borders the Tagus River. Vasco is referencing Toy’s attempts at the ‘<a href=\"/task.php?id=1849\">Eat as much watermelon as possible</a>’ and ‘<a href=\"/task.php?id=3090\">Spread your clothes far and wide</a>’ tasks, respectively.'),
(623, 57, 461, 453, 5, 'Her name stands for television. It stands for production, theatrics, strictness. I know there’s a lot of silliness inside her ready to come out. And this, mother of god, is the right show for that. It’s the unparalleled Teresa Guilherme!', 'Though most recently known for being the long-running host of Portuguese <em>Big Brother</em>, Teresa’s television presenting career has spanned since the early 1990s.'),
(624, 113, 821, 688, 1, 'He makes you question the accuracy of the word ‘celebrity’ in ‘Celebrity Big Brother’: Danick Martineau!', 'Danick won the 4th season of <em>Big Brother Célébrités</em> in 2023.'),
(625, 113, 821, 690, 2, 'She’s the second greatest thing to come out of Drummondville, right after the electric charging station at St-Hubert: Mégan Brouillard!', 'Louis and Mégan are both from the Quebecois city of <a target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Drummondville\">Drummondville</a>, where there is a <a target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/St-Hubert\">St-Hubert</a> brand restaurant with an <a target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://evhype.com/map/location/168624\">EV charging station</a>.'),
(626, 113, 821, 689, 3, 'He’s got your uncle’s clunky cars and your auntie’s laugh: José Gaudet!', 'José is a passionate collector of <a target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=nGhcI-o8E1o\">decidedly not clunky cars</a>.'),
(627, 113, 821, 634, 4, 'Single farmers looking for cheap labour love her. It’s Marie-Soleil Dion!', 'Marie-Soleil hosts <em>L’amour est dans le pré</em> [‘Love is in the field’], the Quebecois adaptation of <em><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Farmer_Wants_a_Wife\">Farmer Wants a Wife</a></em>.'),
(628, 113, 821, 691, 5, 'Few artists are famous enough to be known by only their first name. Céline. Yvon. Véro. And, of course, Neev!', '‘Céline’ is the famous Canadian singer <a target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Celine_Dion\">Céline Dion</a>. ‘Yvon’ is the Quebecois author, actor, comedian and producer <a target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yvon_Deschamps\">Yvon Deschamps</a>. Véro is the Canadian TV and radio personality <a target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/V%C3%A9ronique_Cloutier\">Véronique Cloutier</a>. She also happens to be Louis’ wife.');
